LINES = [{'id': 'rule', 'text': "In this town, on your birthday, you can swap bodies with anyone you want for one day. And they can't say no."}, {'id': 'tickets', 'text': 'Timmy turned nine and picked the Police Chief. He wrote forty tickets for eating broccoli. The real Chief got recess.'}, {'id': 'homework', 'text': 'Jen picked our teacher and canceled homework for a whole year. Miss Park had to take the spelling test.'}, {'id': 'book', 'text': "Every birthday is written in the Birthday Book at Town Hall. Only the Mayor's hand can write in it."}, {'id': 'hide', 'text': "But here's the catch. On your birthday, everybody hides from you, just in case you pick them."}, {'id': 'zero', 'text': 'My parties have had zero guests, three years in a row. Only Grandma Rosa comes, with a cake.'}, {'id': 'never', 'text': "Grandma's had eighty birthdays and never swapped once. She says she's never met anyone she'd rather be."}, {'id': 'preston', 'text': "Then there's Preston. Every birthday, he picks whoever has what he wants. Last year, the bank boss."}, {'id': 'steals', 'text': "At midnight he popped back, with the bank's gold in his bedroom. Eleven birthdays, eleven steals."}, {'id': 'same', 'text': 'This year, Preston and I had the same birthday. At eight a.m., he marched into Town Hall and picked the Mayor.'}, {'id': 'forever', 'text': "He grabbed the Birthday Book and wrote: today is everybody's birthday. Every single day. Forever."}, {'id': 'chaos', 'text': 'So everyone picked everyone. Dad became the baker. The baker became a cop. The cop became Grandma!'}, {'id': 'knees', 'text': 'Nobody could say no, so nobody could stop. Grandma got picked nine times. She just wanted her knees back.'}, {'id': 'brave', 'text': "I hadn't used my swap yet. So I walked into Town Hall, shaking, and picked the Mayor's body. Preston couldn't say no."}, {'id': 'page', 'text': "Then I saw Preston's page. Party guests, every year: zero. If everybody has a birthday, he whispered, nobody hides from me."}, {'id': 'invite', 'text': "So I used the Mayor's hand. I crossed out swap bodies with, and wrote invite."}, {'id': 'party', 'text': "At midnight, everybody popped back. Next morning, our party had three hundred and twelve guests. They couldn't say no."}, {'id': 'slices', 'text': "Grandma cut three hundred and twelve slices. Eighty-one birthdays, still zero swaps. She finally met everyone she'd rather be with."}, {'id': 'callback', 'text': "So now, on your birthday, you can invite anyone you want, and they can't say no. Preston invited the whole town. Twice."}]
